    "summary": "Thinking Machines Lab released Inkling 2 Small, its second-generation Mixture-of-Experts model with 594 billion total parameters and 17 billion active parameters. The model supports image inputs and variable compute effort, achieving a score of 31 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index — surpassing the lab's prior models on agentic coding, vision, knowledge work, and reasoning. According to the company, the gains stem from improvements across the training pipeline, including more efficient pre-training and a large, unified reinforcement-learning run. A companion report notes the model was pre-trained from scratch in under 68 hours on fewer than 12 trillion tokens using native NVFP4 precision, with a single joint RL run, and outperforms Muse Spark. The launch signals that Thinking Machines, after early cofounder departures, has established itself as a high-functioning frontier neolab.",
